WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.828
A form gathers data through named controls.

00:00:02.828 --> 00:00:08.079
Labels explain what to enter, and native input types can provide useful validation.

00:00:08.079 --> 00:00:15.755
Client-side validation improves feedback but cannot establish trust, because a request can be sent without using the page’s form.

00:00:16.755 --> 00:00:17.161
No.

00:00:17.161 --> 00:00:20.000
A caller can construct a request directly.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:27.300
The backend must enforce the same allowed range and reject values such as −1, 101 or a non-number.

00:00:27.300 --> 00:00:30.545
The browser constraints remain useful for ordinary users.

00:00:31.545 --> 00:00:33.733
Where must security-relevant validation run?

00:00:33.733 --> 00:00:38.985
The server must not rely on client-side controls as a security boundary.
